# No trailing slash, for the reason `.venv` below carries in full: in a worktree these are often
# SYMLINKS to the primary checkout's, and `foo/` matches a directory only — which is how a
# mode-120000 entry pointing outside the repository once got committed.
node_modules
dist/
# TypeScript's incremental cache (`tsc -b`), rewritten by every build
*.tsbuildinfo
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# python worker (uv.lock IS committed — the tier has to be reproducible)
# No trailing slash: a worktree's `.venv` is often a SYMLINK to the primary checkout's, and
# `.venv/` matches a directory only — which is how one got committed as a mode-120000 entry
# pointing outside the repository.
.venv
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# The SDD workspace: briefs, per-task reports and review diffs, written by the tooling and never
# part of the build. `.superpowers/sdd/.gitignore` already holds `*`, which covers `sdd/` only and
# is itself a generated file — this covers the directory whatever the tooling puts in it next.
# It matters because a task report quotes what a live run saw, and a live run sees the owner's own
# account.
.superpowers/

# macOS / local scratch
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
# Local test logins left by the old provisioning: never committed.
.test-creds
docs/files/
docs/files.zip

# The owner's box: its address, SSH user and key, SIM (Claude Code's local instructions).
CLAUDE.local.md
# The box's own values the public-tree audit searches for (scripts/audit-public.sh).
scripts/audit-public.local
# Claude Code's per-person settings (permissions, local paths).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Never published: infra/ (how to rebuild the box, a local untracked directory), and what is left
# on the owner's computer of directories deleted from the tree (the TS PoC, its graph data, the
# spec-kit era) — never to be added back. No trailing slash, as above: a worktree's copy may be a
# symlink.
/infra
/old_src
/adapters
/domains
/templates
/specs
/.specify

# Kept on the owner's computer, never published: the deploy (its own private repo), the
# implementation plans, and the product specs that stay private.
/ansible
docs/superpowers/plans
docs/specs/gtm-distribution-spec-en.md
docs/specs/cost-budget-model-spec-en.md
docs/specs/scaling-model-spec-en.md
docs/specs/ai-concierge-design.md
docs/specs/phase1-standalone-runner-spec.md

# Go engine build output
src/engine/bin
# `go build ./cmd/x` in src/engine drops the daemon's binary there
/src/engine/calld
/src/engine/emaild
/src/engine/engine
/src/engine/hostd
/src/engine/secretd
/src/engine/smsd
/src/engine/telegramd
/src/engine/whatsappd
ansible/.build

# Claude Code worktrees (EnterWorktree)
.claude/worktrees

# a plain `go build` in a cmd/ directory leaves its binary there (by name: anything else there is source)
/src/engine/cmd/calld/calld
/src/engine/cmd/emaild/emaild
/src/engine/cmd/engine/engine
/src/engine/cmd/hostd/hostd
/src/engine/cmd/secretd/secretd
/src/engine/cmd/smsd/smsd
/src/engine/cmd/telegramd/telegramd
/src/engine/cmd/whatsappd/whatsappd
